Spleen 8x16, as a PSF2 font
===========================

spleen-8x16.psf is the console font. It was made from spleen-8x16.bdf in
Spleen 2.2.0 (https://github.com/fcambus/spleen/releases/tag/2.2.0) with

    scripts/bdf2psf.py spleen-8x16.bdf vendor/spleen/spleen-8x16.psf

which keeps the 191 printable Latin-1 glyphs (U+0020-U+007E, U+00A0-U+00FF)
and writes a PSF2 file with a Unicode table. Spleen's own .psfu files are
PSF1. kernel/src/font.S embeds the file in the kernel.

